Z||000000||shiloh187||03-30-2001||01:52 AM||||i was looking at that POS i got ripped off on and i noticed something i never saw before..<P>i was looking at the intake thinking of what i wanted to do, and noticed the passengers side does not even have one... threw me off.. so when i buy a custom intake, will the passenger side just be fake like on a rustang?<P>shiloh||||reg||1
Z||000001||DaRkLoRD||03-30-2001||01:58 AM||||A lot of people have cut a hole in the sheet metal and then used the passenger side scoop for engine cooling... air just blows up over the engine and out the vents..<P>------------------<BR>  <A HREF="mailto:steve@fieroproject.com">steve@fieroproject.com</A>  <BR><A HREF="http://www.fieroproject.com" TARGET=_blank>http://www.fieroproject.com</A>||||reg||3
Z||000002||1FST2M6||03-30-2001||09:08 AM||||if you move the battery to the front.. or just remove the battery and remove the insulation behind the battery you'll find a hol already there... (my 87 GT has a hole stamped there... )<P>------------------<BR>    <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/sig1fst.jpg">    <BR>www.engineered.net||||reg||1
Z||000003||shiloh187||03-31-2001||08:15 PM||||how would i move the battery to the front?  would i pick up much horsepower by adding an intake on both sides?<P>shiloh||||reg||1
Z||000004||DXR_DAD||03-31-2001||08:30 PM||||On the V6 it's not so much the HP+ But anything you can to to keep the engine temp down is a +. Deck lid scoop, Side scoops, Remove the grates under the rear vents, Over the roof scoop, all of these will help lower the engine bay temp. Ramair on the driver side that's different and it's been talked about alot. Do a search and get all the info.<BR>Use intake, cold air, side scoops as the search word.<P>DXR_DAD ||||reg||1
